  "result": "I fixed it: shell completion no longer treats a `#` inside an argument as the start of a comment. All 68 tests in the parser and shell-completion suites pass.\n\n- **The fix:** one line in `src/click/shell_completion.py`, `lex.commenters = \"\"`, added in `split_arg_string`. Before this, everything from a `#` onward was dropped, so `cli a#b c` was split as `[\"cli\", \"a\"]` and the completions came out wrong.\n- **Tests:** I added three cases to `test_split_arg_string` in `tests/test_parser.py`: `#foo`, `a#b`, and a quoted `'#a'`. Without the fix, the `#foo` and `a#b` cases fail. The quoted case passes either way, because quoted `#` was already handled correctly.\n- **Changelog:** the changelog is `CHANGES.md`, not `CHANGES.rst` as the plan said. Version 8.5.0 is already marked released, so I added a new \"Version 8.5.1 \u2014 Unreleased\" section for the entry. Adjust the version number if you plan a different release.\n\nNothing is committed yet.",
